{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["I am too small — from having it be mine." "The kindnesses, etc. — and similarly: ״קטן מהכיל את העולה ואת השלמים״. And because You have done for me kindnesses and truth more than is fitting for me, while I have still not fulfilled my vows and have not served You as is fitting, therefore I am afraid — even though You promised me that You do not judge a person except according to his deeds, as we find in the case of Hezekiah, where the prophet said to him: ״מת אתה ולא תחיה״, and nonetheless, through Hezekiah's prayer, the Holy One, blessed be He, added to his days fifteen years."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "The citation קטן מהכיל את העולה ואת השלמים appears to be a rabbinic dictum; left untranslated as Rashbam quotes it without address or source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:00.709366089Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}